misc: add /dev/dtbo, a userspace device tree overlay loader

Writing a compiled overlay to /dev/dtbo applies it to the live tree;
writing "remove <id>" reverts it; reading lists what is applied. Lets a
node be tried on a board that boots a static DTB without reflashing per
attempt.

diff -Nur a/drivers/misc/Kconfig b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig	2026-10-20 12:08:29
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig	2026-10-20 12:08:30
@@ -639,6 +639,17 @@
 
 	  If unsure, say N.
 
+config DTBO_LOADER
+	tristate "Userspace device tree overlay loader (/dev/dtbo)"
+	depends on OF_OVERLAY
+	help
+	  Lets root apply a compiled device tree overlay by writing it to
+	  /dev/dtbo, and revert it by writing "remove <id>". Meant for
+	  bringing up hardware on a board that boots a static device tree:
+	  a node can be tried, corrected and tried again without a reflash.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 config MCHP_LAN966X_PCI
 	tristate "Microchip LAN966x PCIe Support"
 	depends on PCI
